confirm_with_reset.description:
The SmartSlydr API returned a payload the integration didn't recognize — most often an upstream timeout. This can be a backend problem, but a scan interval set too low can also cause it; check **Configure** on the integration page before reporting an outage.

The integration is currently configured with a custom API base URL:

- Current URL: {current_url}
- Default URL: {default_url}

Click Submit to retry. If you suspect the custom URL is the problem, toggle **Reset to default URL** below to revert it before retrying.

The SmartSlydr API has rejected several polls in a row with HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) — Home Assistant is calling it more often than this account's quota allows. Open and close commands share that quota, so your door may stop responding while the limit is in force.

Raise the **Scan interval** under **Configure** on the integration page (default 300 seconds, minimum 30), then wait a few minutes.

The integration is also configured with a custom API base URL:

- Current URL: {current_url}
- Default URL: {default_url}

Click Submit to retry. If you suspect the custom URL is the problem, toggle **Reset to default URL** below to revert it before retrying.

The integration could not contact the SmartSlydr API.

The integration is currently configured with a custom API base URL:

- Current URL: {current_url}
- Default URL: {default_url}

Click Submit to retry. If you suspect the custom URL is the problem, toggle **Reset to default URL** below to revert it before retrying.
